\begin{example}

Generate a summary of the following text: 'Manchester City midfielder Yaya Toure has joined Arsenal on loan until the end of the season. Toure signed for the Gunners on loan after impressing manager Arsene Wenger during his time at Barcelona. Toure signed for the Gunners on loan from Manchester City after impressing manager Arsene Wenger during his time at Barcelona. Wenger is said to be keen to sign the midfielder permanently in the summer.

 If the question had included 'write a summary' then the system should have produced a longer response and should be aware of the purpose of the task to meet the requirements of the customer. This task is a form of machine translation between two languages: summary to the question.  

Question 2 is from the dataset created by Ramponi and Gretter, with the response to be generated being the 'best response' to the question, as determined by the customer. The task requires the system to generate a response that accurately answers the question:

\begin{verbatim}

 The test cases are available in the attachments. The predicted result must be an array of text strings that contains the same text strings that were provided as inputs for the given input texts.

