\section{Conclusion}
In this paper, we presented an overview of NLP techniques to extract knowledge from news articles in order to answer factoid questions, specifically extractive summarization, relation extraction, and NLI. We also provided three different extractive summarization methods (TF-IDF, BERT and BART) to generate the final summary, and two different question answering methods (QA and RNN-LSTM). 
The summarization methods are able to retrieve relevant information for the given question and they are quite efficient.


\end{examples}

\section{Subword-Level Language Model}

In this section, we describe our methods to pre-train a subword-level language model.  Given a tokenization function $t(\cdot)$, we encode a document $D$ into a sequence of wordpiece indices. Let $D=(x_1,...,x_n)$ denote a sequence of wordpieces of length $n$ where $x_i \in \mathbb{R}^d$.
